+
+### XGrammar processor lifecycle
+
+The XGrammar backend uses the tensor library selected by the Transformers
+model. It creates an independent grammar matcher for every batch row and
+advances each matcher with that row's generated tokens. Calling `reset()`
+discards all matcher and token-mask state so that the processor can start a new
+generation. A batch size cannot change during one generation; reset the
+processor before beginning a generation with a different batch size.
